# Send www to the apex. To use it, point a www record at this server, then
# copy this file to caddy.d/www.caddy and reload Caddy (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md,
# "Your own Caddy config").
#
# Record first, file second: Caddy can only get a certificate for a name that
# already resolves, and until the record exists it retries a doomed order for
# as long as the server runs. The record alone does not help either. Caddy
# has no certificate for the name and refuses the TLS handshake, so the
# browser trades an unknown-host error for a connection error.
#
# Redirect rather than serve the app on a second name. Patchwork answers on
# one hostname: session cookies are host-only and every emailed link is built
# from instance.domain, so an instance answering on both would sign someone
# in on one name and mail them links to the other.
www.{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	redir https://{$DOMAIN:localhost}{uri} permanent
}
